    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0123" n="957" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.96/254</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-13T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6571. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 99. Your No. 109. British Embassy has been taking up with us direct matter of
                    eliminating call at Halifax; also, Captain Mackin of British Admiralty, in
                    charge at Halifax, has been here in conference with our naval representatives.
                    Agreement has been reached satisfactory to British Embassy and Captain Mackin,
                    which provides for elimination of call at Halifax by vessels proceeding from
                    United States ports and search at United States ports by United States officials
                    assisted and advised by British Admiralty officers who will be brought here from
                        Halifax.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d39-f1"/> British Embassy and Captain Mackin
                    have cabled Foreign Office and Admiralty respectively asking their approval of
                    foregoing arrangements. Upon securing such approval we understand call at
                    Halifax will at once be eliminated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d39-f1" n="1" xml:id="d39-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram to the Ambassador in Great Britain, June 14, No. 8270, for Sheldon, No.
                    679, states: “Present arrangement with the British Government … provides for a
                    search in United States ports of only those vessels which load their [entire]
                    cargoes in the United States.” (File No. 656.119/484.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
